@local/dsh-mcp-status README · Installation：2. Enable the bundle. The supported path is the DSH plugin manager
   (Settings → Plugins: enable `@local/dsh-mcp-status`); it edits the profile
   manifest for you. By hand it is the same bundle list:

```json
   "dsh": {
     "profile": {
       "bundles": ["@deepseek-ai/dsh-base", "@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-app", "@local/dsh-mcp-status"]
     }

3. Restart DSH. The host half activates with the profile; the client half
   appears on the next page load.

@local/dsh-mcp-status README · Troubleshooting：`.activation.log` next to the package records `import` (module loaded),
`apply-start` (loader row mounted), `route-registered`, and `effect-error` (what
threw). It is git-ignored.
